think r1 and r2 landed and pushed (nib 266b8cbfa8). r3 on the Statement arc is "across a Knot" — reading one account's line over a checkpoint-continued ledger, mirroring lapse_knot/pledge_knot/braid_knot.
think Studied mycelium/lapse_knot.rye: a LapseKnot seals a committed prefix (cord_knot.seal_dag) and carries the epoch base (committed_len) so continue_lapse folds the suffix at absolute positions base+i — the deadline clock never restarts at the cut. Its lapses_match compares the whole Cord against the Knot-plus-suffix and they agree.
think The Statement's r3 crux is simpler than the Lapse's: it composes statement.statement_for over both paths (resolve_whole vs seal_lapse+continue_lapse) and proves statements_match — the account's line does not drift at the checkpoint, position and pledge lines and reconciliation identical. The honest seam the Statement itself meets across a Knot: received (cumulative inflow) must accumulate across the base, not restart. Because continue_lapse seeds its ledger with the prefix account map (received intact) and suffix credits add onto it, the Statement reads received continuous — exercised by a far-deadline (5) pledge honored in the suffix, so Bob (absent at the seal) reads his whole 100 inflow.
obs GREEN on the first run. Two scenes: deadline 2 (pledge lapses across the cut; Alice's and Bob's statements match whole vs across, Alice reconciles, her made line reads lapsed) and deadline 5 (honored across the cut; Bob's received reads 100 not a restart, Alice's reserved returns, both match and reconcile). One integrity refusal: a Knot corrupted after sealing refuses KnotCorrupt before any statement is read — a line is never read from a tampered checkpoint.
obs Additive — composes statement + lapse_knot + lapse + cord + fold public API only, edited no module; the Statement r1 and the Lapse-Knot re-run GREEN at the witness door. TAME bans clean (statement_knot.rye not flagged), width-check clean.
